      },
      {
        "Id": "83cc1b4e661c4409b465de75ec17dfce",
        "Title": "HOW TO USE:  in Revit SELECT the stair source first - ONE line = guide line (direction + run length), the LINES of a closed shaft outline (rectangle / polygon, Revit or CAD), or a Room / Area (or leave nothing selected: the Area / Room named STAIR is used). Then set the mode (3: floor to floor / all levels / selected levels / continuous), the configuration (7) and the sizes. ACTION (20): VALIDATE = checks only (riser, tread, landings, headroom, floor opening, clashes) | PREVIEW = builds, reports, rolls back | GENERATE = builds the native Revit stair (runs + landings + railings) | UPDATE = select the generated stair(s): rebuilt from the stored shaft / room + settings | DELETE = selected source / stair, or all generated stairs. Run again = replaced (no doubles). Spiral is not built.",
        "DescriptionText": "",
        "IsExpanded": true,
        "WidthAdjustment": 0.0,
        "HeightAdjustment": 0.0,
        "Nodes": [],
        "HasNestedGroups": false,
